# Server / Client Boundaries (SR-App)

Detailed reference: `docs/steering/technical/server-client-boundaries.md`.

**Hard rules**
- **Default to Server Components.** Add `"use client"` only for real interactivity (forms w/ local state, maps, camera/upload, timers, offline queue, charts).
- **Data fetching on the server** (RSC or server actions); client components get data via props/actions — no direct DB access, no secrets client-side.
- **Trust boundary = server:** every action/handler re-validates input (Zod) + re-checks authorization regardless of the client.
- **No secrets/tokens/keys in client bundles** — only `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` may reach the client.
- Client components stay **leaf-level and small**; push data/logic to the server.
- Presigned upload URLs are minted server-side; the client uses but can't mint them.

**Guidance:** pattern = server page → fetch + authorize → minimal props → small client island. Co-locate feature server actions in `lib/<feature>/actions.ts` (`"use server"`).

**DoD:** interactivity isolated to small client islands; data/authz server-side; no secrets on client; mutations re-validate + re-authorize on the server.
